SECURE. #C914 v2 on 7c16281 (replaces e1687185). stack-queue.json is written by the probe's atomic 0600 writer and holds ids, regex-checked owner_role and repo words, dependency ids, a started flag and a time, at most 500 cards; no secret. stack-ready.mjs reads it read-only, with no network or token; its config comes from --config or BOARD_CONFIG only. Git runs through execFileSync with fixed arrays and no shell. stackHold is true only. A stack-ready note can only release a hold (only the 40-hex annotated sha is read). A missing or stale queue means the note is written, i.e. an early review. A backdated commit escaping STACK_HOLD_FROM also means only an early review. The depends_on relaxation applies only with the switch on, to board cards of the same owner_role, and only for a pushed dependency; ship signatures are untouched. The reset.mjs wake line is constant text plus a boolean. LOW carried over from v1, still open: stack-ready.mjs pushes HEAD from any branch, main included, and flight-board's pre-push hook does not guard main; refusing main closes it.
